192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Placing a persistent call-to-action button on the right side of the screen is based on established user behavior patterns and UI research showing that accessibility and visibility directly impact conversion rates.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Most users scan websites in an F-shaped or Z-shaped reading pattern, meaning they tend to focus on the top and right areas of the screen after initial content scanning. Keeping a CTA fixed on the right ensures it stays within this natural visual flow, making it easier to notice without interrupting reading.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
